  "term": "glutamatergic",
  "definition": "Glutamatergic refers to brain pathways or mechanisms involving glutamate as part of how neural circuits function. In this psychiatry context, it names one of the non-dopamine pathways being explored to understand and treat schizophrenia within a broader, circuit-based view.",
