      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “glutamatergic” as involving glutamate (it only mentions “glutamatergic pathways” without stating that glutamate is the mechanism).",
        "The packet supports that “glutamatergic pathways” are part of a “shift beyond dopamine dominance” and a “circuit-level integration” in schizophrenia, but it does not clearly support the definition’s claim that these pathways are “being explored to understand and treat schizophrenia.”",
        "The definition asserts a specific “non-dopamine pathways” framing for glutamatergic mechanisms within a broader circuit-based view; while dopamine is discussed and non-dopamine mechanisms are implied, the packet does not unambiguously establish glutamatergic as one of the explicitly named “non-dopamine” pathways for treatment in the precise way stated."
